   "id": "a02f12ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "opioids_deaths = pd.read_csv(\"data/opioids_deaths.csv\")\n",
    "opioids_deaths = opioids_deaths.copy()\n",
    "opioids_deaths = opioids_deaths.drop(columns=[\"Unnamed: 0\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9c8e168f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Control States"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3d328c11",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> ### NOTE:\n",
    "> Based off the analysis found in `opioid_project_analysis.ipynb`, ['MICHIGAN', 'PENNSYLVANIA', 'TENNESSEE'] may be reasonable control states to explore average population size, overdose trends, and prescription shipment trends before 2010. However, these three states together don't seem to do well in the plots below.\n",
    ">\n",
    "> There's also the top 10 states that have similar:\n",
    "> - **prescription shipment trend as pre 2010 Florida:** ['NEW YORK', 'NEVADA', 'PENNSYLVANIA', 'CALIFORNIA', 'NEW JERSEY', 'VIRGINIA', 'RHODE ISLAND', 'MISSISSIPPI', 'MARYLAND']\n",
    "> -  **overdose trend as pre 2010 Florida:** ['NORTH DAKOTA', 'SOUTH DAKOTA', 'WYOMING', 'MARYLAND', 'ILLINOIS', 'IDAHO', 'NEW YORK', 'CONNECTICUT', 'COLORADO']"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b4a68899",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# right now, using 2 different sets of control states for prescription shipments and overdose\n",
    "\n",
    "# control states for prescription shipments: Ohio, Alabama, Georgia, Kentucky\n",
    "control_states_prescriptions = [\n",
    "    \"OHIO\",\n",
    "    \"ALABAMA\",\n",
    "    \"GEORGIA\",\n",
    "    \"KENTUCKY\",\n",
    "]\n",
    "opioids_states_prescriptions = opioids_prescriptions[\n",
    "    opioids_prescriptions[\"state\"].isin(control_states_prescriptions + [\"FLORIDA\"])\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# control states for overdoses: Colorado, Michigan, Pennsylvania\n",
    "control_states_od = [\"COLORADO\", \"MICHIGAN\", \"PENNSYLVANIA\"]\n",
    "opioids_states_od = opioids_deaths[\n",
    "    opioids_deaths[\"state\"].isin(control_states_od + [\"FLORIDA\"])\n",
    "]"
   ]
  },
  {
